# auferstehung - Gustav Mahler, Symphony No. 2 in C minor, the finale
# (fifth movement), from "Bereite dich" (after 43) toward the close.
# Source: the first edition of the full score, Leipzig: Friedrich
# Hofmeister, 1897 (University of Toronto copy, Internet Archive
# `symphonieno200mahl`), printed pages 196-201, 204 and 209. Public
# domain: published 1897; Mahler died in 1911. Arranged for pax's
# speaker by its px29 lane: one slot a beat, the voices that sing in it
# as a chord (at most four; the speaker sounds a chord as an arpeggio).
#
# Carried: 43+6 to the end of p. 201 (chorus, then the alto and soprano
# soloists from 44 and 45, the chorus's canon from 46), then 48 bars
# 1-8 and 51 to the end. NOT carried, because not verified bar by bar:
# p. 202 to 48 (about 15 bars: "werde ich entschweben", 47 "Sterben
# werd' ich") and 48 bar 9 to 50 bar 12 (about 35 bars). Those are a
# cut, not a guess. notes/px29/reduction.md lists every doubt.
